From 268fa07c5a87679ceba7866669aab893968afd49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix(pathkernel): refuse an unoriented centre and keep
 the geometry error kind

The region builder no longer makes an unoriented cutter-centre area normal again: PlanarRegion::new refuses it with NOT_ORIENTED (guard pinned on the loops). The four geo() helpers keep the kind of a GeoError (<STAGE>_GEOMETRY for OutOfRange, <STAGE>_GEOMETRY_INVALID for Invalid). A ring piece that Curve::new refuses for a reason other than too short is a refusal, not dropped.

Refs #4407
Refs #4383

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
